---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const upworkUrl = 'https://www.upwork.com/services/product/writing-translation-professional-sops-and-clear-process-documentation-2098097452881572813?ref=project_share';
---
<BaseLayout title="Selected Project Work" current="" description="Selected short-term project services from Richard J. Allen, including SOP development, workflow documentation, training and onboarding guides, support procedures, and documentation cleanup.">
<section class="page-intro"><div class="container">
  <div class="eyebrow">Selected Project Work</div>
  <h1>Clear documentation for work that matters.</h1>
  <p class="lede">My primary focus is finding the right long-term operations or customer-success leadership role. I also take on selected, well-defined short-term projects when a team needs an important process documented, organized, or made easier to use.</p>
  <div class="actions"><a class="button" href="mailto:rjallencareer@gmail.com?subject=Project%20work%20inquiry">Discuss a project</a><a class="button secondary" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href={upworkUrl}>View Upwork SOP service</a></div>
</div></section>

<section class="section"><div class="container">
  <div class="section-heading-row"><div><div class="eyebrow">Focused services</div><h2>Small, practical scopes built around proven experience.</h2></div><p class="section-note">I keep project work close to areas I have actually done in operations, support, training, customer experience, and process improvement.</p></div>
  <div class="grid two value-grid">
    <article class="card accent-teal"><div class="card-icon">SOP</div><h3>SOP creation & standardization</h3><p>Turn notes, screenshots, forms, interviews, and existing materials into clear Standard Operating Procedures with consistent structure and ownership.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-blue"><div class="card-icon">FLOW</div><h3>Process & workflow documentation</h3><p>Document who does what, when, with which inputs, systems, handoffs, decisions, and escalation points.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-gold"><div class="card-icon">LEARN</div><h3>Training & onboarding guides</h3><p>Create practical instructions and reference material that help employees or customers learn a process and repeat it consistently.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-violet"><div class="card-icon">OPS</div><h3>Support-operations procedures</h3><p>Document customer-support, troubleshooting, escalation, service, handoff, quality, and related operating procedures.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-teal"><div class="card-icon">FIX</div><h3>Existing-document cleanup</h3><p>Review older procedures for unclear language, inconsistent structure, duplicated material, gaps, missing ownership, and difficult-to-follow steps.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-blue"><div class="card-icon">GOV</div><h3>Documentation governance</h3><p>Help organize standards, repositories, review practices, and maintenance guidelines so documentation stays useful after the initial project ends.</p></article>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="section impact-section"><div class="container">
  <div class="section-heading-row"><div><div class="eyebrow">Why this is a natural fit</div><h2>Project services grounded in actual operating work.</h2></div></div>
  <div class="grid two value-grid">
    <article class="card accent-gold"><h3>Year-long SOP program leadership</h3><p>Led/co-led an Oregon Employment Department modernization and governance program across roughly 10 functional groups. The work included inventorying and updating 25+ legacy procedures, documenting missing processes, standardizing templates and review controls, coaching contributors, and centralizing a library that ultimately identified, created, and collected 100+ SOPs.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-blue"><h3>Procedures across sales and support</h3><p>Historical HawkSoft records show creation, updating, and documentation of dozens of sales policies and procedures in addition to customer-support, technical-support, training, and operating documentation.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-teal"><h3>Product & training documentation</h3><p>At The Kotter Group, documented Bridge XLerator features and benefits, usage instructions, user stories and business cases; also created customer education, release/procedure documentation, webinars, and training content.</p></article>
    <article class="card accent-violet"><h3>Operations perspective</h3><p>Documentation work is informed by experience managing people, workflows, reporting, quality, change, customer operations, warehouse/supply operations, and cross-functional execution—not documentation in isolation.</p></article>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="section project-services"><div class="container">
  <div class="project-service-panel">
    <div>
      <div class="eyebrow">Upwork Project Catalog</div>
      <h2>Professional SOPs & clear process documentation</h2>
      <p class="project-service-lede">My Upwork freelancer profile and SOP-focused Project Catalog service were approved and published in September 2026. Upwork provides a convenient way to purchase a defined documentation project; direct project inquiries are also welcome.</p>
      <p class="small">No freelance client ratings, earnings, or completed-project outcomes are presented here yet because this is a new project-work channel.</p>
    </div>
    <aside class="project-proof">
      <div class="eyebrow">Two ways to start</div>
      <div class="actions"><a class="button" href="mailto:rjallencareer@gmail.com?subject=Project%20work%20inquiry">Email about a project</a><a class="button secondary" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href={upworkUrl}>View Upwork service</a></div>
    </aside>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="section tight"><div class="container"><div class="callout"><strong>Full-time opportunities remain my primary focus.</strong> Project work is a complementary option for organizations that need a defined piece of operational documentation or enablement work completed now. <a href="/contact/">Contact me about a role or project →</a></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
